# Ashiok, Dream Render forbids only a spell that makes its own controller search their own library. Two controls for the
# edges of that text (Bot1 controls Ashiok; Bot2 is the opponent). Bot2's Winds of Abandon exiles Bot1's Ornithopter, so Bot1,
# not the spell's controller, searches Bot1's library for a basic land: allowed (the ruling: opponents' spells "may cause other
# players to search their libraries"). Then, on turn 4 (the Moxen untapped), Bot2's Ancient Vendetta names Island, so Bot2 searches Bot1's library, not
# its own ("their library"): allowed, and it finds two Islands in the
# library and, by default, the one in Bot1's hand, which are exiled with the Ornithopter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Ashiok, Dream Render
Ornithopter
Plains x2
Plains x4
Island x2
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Winds of Abandon
Ancient Vendetta
Plains x3
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ashiok, Dream Render.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Winds of Abandon.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Search(Plains)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ancient Vendetta.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Name(Island)
Bot2.Search(Island; Island)

[Expect]
Turn = 4
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Ashiok, Dream Render; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Sapphire; Plains
Exile = Island; Island; Island; Ornithopter
